    <section class="sect reveal flush">
      <div class="kicker">Reassurance</div>
      <h2>What carries forward.</h2>
      <p class="sdek">The names change; the muscle memory doesn't. Three things move with you.</p>
      <div class="three">
        <div class="card"><h3>Your rooms</h3><p>Mersive Solstice Gen 3 hardware has a mapped transition path: supported through 2029, with a trade-in program in motion. Polaris Pro continues the line your rooms already run.</p><a href="/products/transition">The transition path →</a></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Your workflows</h3><p>Walk up, share, sources side by side on the display. The habits your users built on Mersive Solstice work the same on Polaris. The workspace simply evolved around them: web-join, the Dock, cross-network reach.</p><a href="/platform/how">Meet Polaris →</a></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Your management</h3><p>Mersive Solstice Cloud keeps running your Gen 3 units exactly as today, linked straight from Polaris Cloud: one starting point while rooms move generation by generation, with none of the tooling your team knows going dark. [Unified in-pane claim retired pending cloud-team confirmation.]</p><a href="/platform/cloud">Polaris Cloud →</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="mdna reveal">
      <h3>Why the name?</h3>
      <p>Mersive Solstice was named for the sky, and so is its successor. Polaris is the fixed point the whole northern sky turns around, the star every navigator steers by. Fifteen years of Mersive Solstice taught rooms to share wirelessly; Polaris is the generation where the room itself joins, hosts, and carries the meeting, the one reliable point in a shifting sky of platforms, networks, and devices.</p>
      <p class="concede">One company, one mission, one platform generation to the next. The name is the promise, in writing: whatever the meeting runs on, the room holds steady.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="g3band reveal"><b>Mersive Solstice Gen 3 owner?</b> Your platform is supported, documented, and has a mapped road ahead; nothing here is a surprise deprecation. <span class="btns"><a class="btn accent" href="/products/solstice">Mersive Solstice today →</a><a class="btn accent" href="/products/transition">Mersive Solstice Gen 3 → Polaris →</a></span></div>
    <div class="g3band reveal" style="background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(47,138,168,.16),rgba(124,227,168,.08));border-color:#2f6a80"><b>New to Mersive?</b> Skip the history. Start with the family and pick the tier your rooms need. <span class="btns"><a class="btn accent" href="/products/family">The Polaris family →</a></span></div>
    <CtaBand variant="story" />
</BaseLayout>
